---
/**
 * Track 11 (Neural Network Intuition), Lesson 2, illustration 3 of 5.
 *
 * The output layer as a bar chart. Ten neurons, one per digit 0 to 9, each
 * holding a confidence score. Using the lesson's exact activations, the 3
 * neuron towers at 0.92 and every other bar is tiny. Reading the output is
 * just finding the tallest bar.
 */
const acts = [0.02, 0.01, 0.05, 0.92, 0.03, 0.04, 0.01, 0.02, 0.01, 0.02];
const baseY = 250;
const maxH = 196;
const barW = 40;
const step = 58;
const startX = 64;
const bars = acts.map((a, i) => ({
	digit: i,
	a,
	x: startX + i * step,
	h: a * maxH,
	top: baseY - a * maxH,
	winner: i === 3,
}));
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 660 320" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="nn-out-title nn-out-desc">
		<title id="nn-out-title">The output layer reads as a bar chart, with the digit 3 the tallest</title>
		<desc id="nn-out-desc">Ten bars, one per output neuron labeled 0 through 9, drawn as a bar chart of activations. The bar for the digit 3 towers at 0.92 and is highlighted in violet. Every other bar is tiny, between 0.01 and 0.05. The tallest bar is the network's guess, so the answer is 3, and the high value means the network is confident.</desc>

		<defs>
			<marker id="nn-out-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#7c3aed" /></marker>
		</defs>

		<line x1="48" y1={baseY} x2="636" y2={baseY} stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" opacity="0.4" />

		{bars.map((b) => (
			<g>
				<rect x={b.x} y={b.top} width={barW} height={b.h} rx="2" fill={b.winner ? '#7c3aed' : 'currentColor'} opacity={b.winner ? 0.9 : 0.32} />
				<text x={b.x + barW / 2} y={b.top - 7} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="11" font-weight={b.winner ? 700 : 400} fill={b.winner ? '#7c3aed' : 'currentColor'} opacity={b.winner ? 1 : 0.7}>{b.a.toFixed(2)}</text>
				<text x={b.x + barW / 2} y={baseY + 20} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight={b.winner ? 700 : 400} fill="currentColor" opacity={b.winner ? 1 : 0.7}>{b.digit}</text>
			</g>
		))}

		<text x="40" y={baseY + 20} text-anchor="end" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.55">digit</text>
		<text x="300" y="36" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" fill="#7c3aed" font-weight="600">tallest bar wins: the guess is 3</text>
		<line x1="300" y1="44" x2={startX + 3 * step + barW / 2} y2={baseY - 0.92 * maxH - 22} stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="1.25" marker-end="url(#nn-out-arrow)" opacity="0.8" />
		<text x="300" y="300" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">activation = confidence (0 to 1)</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>After the network does its work, each of the ten output neurons holds a confidence score. Here the 3 neuron holds 0.92, far above the rest, so the answer is "3" and the high value says the network is confident. If two bars were close, say 0.45 and 0.43, that would be the network hesitating between two digits.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 660px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
